The issue is confirmed in the `FunctionTool.__call__` method in 
`src/agentscope/tool/_adapters.py`. The method returns the direct result of the 
wrapped function call, which can be a plain string, but it needs to be a 
`ToolChunk` or an async generator of `ToolChunk` objects according to the 
AgentScope tooling requirements.

To fix this issue, I will modify `FunctionTool.__call__` to normalize the return
value so that:
- If the returned value is a `ToolChunk` or an async generator of `ToolChunk` 
objects, return as is.
- If it is a plain string, wrap it in a `ToolChunk`.
- Handle other types gracefully, potentially by also converting them into an 
appropriate `ToolChunk`.

